// Image binary - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A raw image is pixels with no header, so the format has to be agreed
# out of band. "Hello World!" as 8-bit grey pixels is this bit stream,
# 96 pixels, 96 bytes, no padding and nothing else to read:
48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21
